==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Could be really good when paired with good stunning fruits such as [[Ice]], [[Dark]], [[Lightning]], etc.
* High damage.
* Excellent for beginners.
* All moves can damage large objects.
* Good combo potential.
** Both skills combo into each other.
* Low mastery requirements.

|'''[Z] One Thousand Slices'''
* Stuns the enemy for an approximate duration of ~1 sec.
* Decent range.
* No needed [[mastery]].

|'''[X] Dark Air Slash'''
* Has extremely long range.
* Very fast. (If held)
* Low mastery.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* [[Blade]] is immune to it.
* Very expensive to obtain.
** Costs ≈$15 (USD)/£10/€12 to obtain, unless the player obtained the {{Robux|Robux}} from a premium payout or got it from [[trading]]/getting gifted it.
* Does not have a lot of [[combos]], and it instead depends a lot on reaction time and skills most of the time.
* Dash move on the fourth click move.

|'''[Z] One Thousand Slices'''
* Poor mobility.

|'''[X] Dark Air Slash'''
* Predictable if not held.
* When holding this move, the opponent could punish the user by getting close with fast [[teleportation]] moves and start a [[Combos|combo]].
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* The Dark Blade's in-game icon is inaccurate, as ever since the change to [[Aura]] in [[Updates/24|Update 24]], the sword no longer lights up.
* The Dark Blade makes the user spin when they do an [[Air Jump]] or side [[Dashing|dash]]. The user will also do a roll when they back dash.
* The Dark Blade was previously called the "Yoru", which was then changed to Dark Blade.
* There is a triple version of the Dark Blade, named the [[Triple Dark Blade]].
** This version is only usable by admins or people they granted it to.
* The Dark Blade is the only [[sword]] that requires obtaining a [[Game Pass]] to obtain.
* The [[Brazil Cube]] allowed the first player who touched it to receive Dark Blade. However, it could only be spawned in by an admin.
* The Dark Blade is one of the few items in the game to have its [[rarity]] altered.
* The Dark Blade is often abbreviated as "DB". ''Check [[Dictionary]] for more info about such abbreviations.''
* The Dark Blade is recommended for all seas as it has high damage, low mastery requirements, and is comparable to swords like [[Cursed Dual Katana]], [[True Triple Katana]], or [[Shark Anchor]].
* Unlike other swords and weapons, Dark Blade's idle does not overlap with custom idles.
* The Dark Blade and [[Dog Blade]] are currently the only tradable swords in the game.
* The Dark Blade is the first sword obtained by a gamepass. It is also the first sword obtained by a gamepass with skins.
* Dark Blade's loss of lighting up is confirmed to be a 'low priority bug' by Admin E, meaning it is not intentional.
* There is a myth where defeating [[Rip indra]] will drop a Dark Blade, but it is impossible to confirm. 
